  "title": "Business-day close blocker parity across preview, enforcement and owner attention",
  "scope": "Bounded comparison of read-only close-blocker preview, actual close admission, owner-dashboard blocker count, shared evaluator, route wiring and the integration test that compares preview to a close attempt.",
  "decision": "PreviewCloseBlockersAsync, CloseBusinessDayHandler and OwnerDashboardQueryService all call BusinessDayCloseEvaluator.EvaluateAsync. The GET and close routes bind to those consumers; the existing integration test opens a shift, checks OPEN_SHIFT in preview, attempts close, and asserts identical blocker-code sets. This is shared logic, not independently duplicated blocker rules; no divergence or new finding confirmed. Evaluator inputs include global outstanding shifts/custodies/journal entries/pending electronic payments and global protected balances, while checklist and some discrepancy checks are business-day scoped. Global-vs-day closure policy needs explicit owner/system scope confirmation, but source alone does not establish a defect; deployment topology may intentionally allow only one active day.",
