  "counterevidence_and_limits": [
    "BusinessDayRules.Open rejects opening while any active business day exists; this supports a single-active-day design, but does not alone prove stale historical obligations should be global blockers.",
    "Preview/close parity test exists in source but was not executed in this audit.",
    "The source does not document whether close blockers for shifts, custodies, journals and pending electronic payments should be day-specific or global; no new finding is created without that policy.",
    "SQL transaction isolation, cross-day fixtures and actual dashboard responses were not tested."
  ],
  "recommendation": "Keep one shared evaluator as the authoritative blocker calculation. Before future scoping changes, document whether non-checklist blockers represent global unresolved financial obligations or only obligations attached to the target business day; test another-date open shift, custody, incomplete journal and pending payment, plus dashboard/preview/close parity under the selected rule.",
